        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Every fraction represents a division - the division of the numerator by the denominator. For example:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}3} = {\\color{blue}1} \\div {\\color{red}3}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Every fraction represents a division - the division of the numerator by the denominator. For example:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}3} = {\\color{blue}1} \\div {\\color{red}3}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Likewise, we can represent every division problem as a fraction, where the dividend is the numerator, and the divisor is the denominator. For example:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Likewise, we can represent every division problem as a fraction, where the dividend is the numerator, and the divisor is the denominator. For example:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}3} \\div {\\color{red}2} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}2}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: {\\color{blue}3} \\div {\\color{red}2} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}2}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nEvery fraction represents a division - the division of the numerator by the denominator. For example:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}3} = {\\color{blue}1} \\div {\\color{red}3}]\n\nContent:\nLikewise, we can represent every division problem as a fraction, where the dividend is the numerator, and the divisor is the denominator. For example:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}3} \\div {\\color{red}2} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}2}]"
      },
      {
