        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 59\\div 4]</span> as a fraction.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Express [MATH: 59\\div 4] as a fraction.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>A division problem may be interpreted as a fraction, where the dividend is the numerator, and the divisor is the denominator.</p><p>Therefore, we can represent the given division problem as </p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 59\\div 4=\\dfrac{59}{4}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "A division problem may be interpreted as a fraction, where the dividend is the numerator, and the divisor is the denominator.\n\nTherefore, we can represent the given division problem as\n\n[MATH: 59\\div 4=\\dfrac{59}{4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: 59\\div 4] as a fraction.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nA division problem may be interpreted as a fraction, where the dividend is the numerator, and the divisor is the denominator.\n\nTherefore, we can represent the given division problem as\n\n[MATH: 59\\div 4=\\dfrac{59}{4}.]"
      },
