          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we can represent the given division problem as a fraction:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 20\\div 8 = \\dfrac{20}{8}]</span></p><p>Then, we can simplify the fraction by dividing both the numerator and denominator by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{20\\div 4}{8\\div 4} = \\dfrac{5}{2}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we can represent the given division problem as a fraction:\n\n[MATH: 20\\div 8 = \\dfrac{20}{8}]\n\nThen, we can simplify the fraction by dividing both the numerator and denominator by [MATH: 4\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{20\\div 4}{8\\div 4} = \\dfrac{5}{2}]",
